1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,140
MAN: Good morning, Kenton Festival box office. How can I help you?

2
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:12,776
WOMAN: Oh, good morning. I'm coming to Kenton for a few days' holiday next month,

3
00:00:12,776 --> 00:00:16,100
and a friend told me there's a festival

4
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:19,540
She gave me this number to find out about it.

5
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:26,880
MAN: That's right, the festival begins on the 16th of May and goes on till the 19th.

6
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:32,272
WOMAN: Oh, that's great. I'll be there from the 15th till the 19th.

7
00:00:32,272 --> 00:00:35,590
So could you tell me the programme, please?

8
00:00:35,590 --> 00:00:42,033
MAN: Well, on the first day, there's the opening ceremony, in the town centre.

9
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:44,795
People start gathering around 2 o'clock,

10
00:00:44,795 --> 00:00:50,240
to get a good place to see from, and the events will start at 2

11
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:54,460
45, and finish about 5.30.

12
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:59,770
WOMAN: OK, thanks. I'll make sure I get there early to get a good spot.

13
00:00:59,770 --> 00:01:04,114
MAN: The festival will be officially opened by the mayor.

14
00:01:04,114 --> 00:01:09,328
He'll just speak for a few minutes, welcoming everyone to the festival.

15
00:01:09,328 --> 00:01:15,410
All the town councillors will be there, and of course lots of other people.

16
00:01:15,410 --> 00:01:17,110
WOMAN: Right.

17
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:20,840
MAN: Then there'll be a performance by a band

18
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:24,129
Most years we have a children's choir,

19
00:01:24,129 --> 00:01:30,270
but this year the local army cadets offered to perform, and they're very good.

20
00:01:30,270 --> 00:01:31,700
WOMAN: Uhuh.

21
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:38,530
MAN: After that, a community group from the town will perform a play they've written themselves,

22
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:45,360
just a short one. It's about Helen Tungate. I don't know if you've heard of her?

23
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:50,480
WOMAN: I certainly have. She was a scientist years ago.

24
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:56,160
MAN: That's right. She was born in Kenton exactly 100 years ago

25
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:59,380
so we're celebrating her centenary.

26
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:03,360
WOMAN: I'm a biologist, so I've always been interested in her

27
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:06,610
I didn't realise she came from Kenton.

28
00:02:06,610 --> 00:02:11,560
MAN: Yes. Well, all that will take place in the afternoon

29
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:13,616
and later, as the sun sets,

30
00:02:13,616 --> 00:02:16,260
there'll be a firework display

31
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:22,270
You should go to the park to watch, as you'll get the best view from there.

32
00:02:22,270 --> 00:02:26,642
And the display takes place on the opposite side of the river.

33
00:02:26,642 --> 00:02:30,650
It's always one of the most popular events in the festival.

34
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:32,890
WOMAN: Sounds great.

35
00:02:32,890 --> 00:02:36,160
WOMAN: And what's happening on the other days?

36
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:41,269
MAN: There are several events that go on the whole time.

37
00:02:41,269 --> 00:02:47,770
For example, the students of the art college have produced a number of videos,

38
00:02:47,770 --> 00:02:51,950
all connected with relationships between children and their grandparents.

39
00:02:51,950 --> 00:02:58,490
WOMAN: That sounds interesting. It makes a change from children and parents, doesn't it!

40
00:02:58,490 --> 00:03:04,225
MAN: Exactly. Because the art college is in use for classes,

41
00:03:04,225 --> 00:03:09,960
throughout the festival, the videos are being shown in Handsworth House.

42
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:12,350
WOMAN: How do you spell the name?

43
00:03:12,350 --> 00:03:24,700
MAN: H-A-N-D-S-W-O-R-T-H. Handsworth House. It's close to the Town Hall.

44
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:26,050
WOMAN: Right.

45
00:03:26,050 --> 00:03:31,000
MAN: Now let me see, what else can I tell you about?

46
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,160
WOMAN: Are there any displays of ballet dancing

47
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:38,670
I'm particularly interested in that as I do it as a hobby.

48
00:03:38,670 --> 00:03:40,860
MAN: There isn't any ballet,

49
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:47,430
I'm afraid, but there'll be a demonstration of traditional dances from all round the country.

50
00:03:47,430 --> 00:03:51,420
WOMAN: Oh, that'd be nice. Where's that being held?

51
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:54,600
MAN: It's in the market in the town centre

52
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:58,484
the outdoor one, not the covered market.

53
00:03:58,484 --> 00:04:05,990
And it's on at 2 and 5 every afternoon of the festival, apart from the first day.

54
00:04:05,990 --> 00:04:12,580
WOMAN: Lovely. I'm interested in all kinds of dancing, so I'm sure I'll enjoy that!

55
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:14,790
MAN: Mmm. I'm sure you will.

56
00:04:14,790 --> 00:04:19,480
WOMAN: And I'd really like to go to some concerts, if there are any.

57
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:24,340
MAN: Yes, there are several. Three performed by professionals

58
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:26,990
and one by local children.

59
00:04:26,990 --> 00:04:29,630
WOMAN: And where is it being held?

60
00:04:29,630 --> 00:04:33,600
MAN: It's in the library, which is in Park Street

61
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:38,410
On the 18th, at 6.30 in the evening.

62
00:04:38,410 --> 00:04:41,670
WOMAN: I presume I'll need tickets for that.

63
00:04:41,670 --> 00:04:48,520
MAN: Yes. You can book online, or you can buy them when you arrive in Kenton.

64
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:50,380
Either at the festival box office

65
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:55,370
or from any shops displaying our logo in the windows.

66
00:04:55,370 --> 00:05:00,997
WOMAN: Well. I think that'll keep me busy for the whole of my stay in Kenton.

67
00:05:00,997 --> 00:05:03,810
Thank you so much for all your help.

68
00:05:03,810 --> 00:05:07,830
MAN: You're welcome. I hope you enjoy your stay.

69
00:05:07,830 --> 00:05:10,740
WOMAN: Thank you. Goodbye.
